- Burnell, J.G. (1947). Flow of boiling water through nozzles, orifices, and pipes. *Engineering*, 164, 572.
- Dyer, J., Doran, E., Dunn, Z., Lohner, K., Zilliac, G., Cantwell, B. (2007). Modeling feed system flow physics for self-pressurizing propellants. AIAA 2007-5702.
- Bell, I.H., Wronski, J., Quoilin, S., Lemort, V. (2014). Pure and pseudo-pure fluid thermophysical property evaluation and the open-source thermophysical property library CoolProp. *Industrial & Engineering Chemistry Research*, 53(6), 2498–2508.

## Development notes

This was my first Python project, written to learn the language through a real fluid-mechanics application. AI assistance was used for this readme, syntax, commenting, code structure, and debugging; the model implementations, validation approach, and interpretation of results are my own.